+# HARNESS_LOG — dasha predictions error
+
+## Plan
+- Report: opening dasha predictions shows an error; worked before, broke recently.
+- Read: app/api/dasha/route.ts, lib/claude.ts, lib/constants.ts, lib/claude-json-reply.test.ts, lib/claude-models.test.ts.
+- Finding: `generateDashaPrediction` (lib/claude.ts) still sends an assistant prefill
+  (`{ role: "assistant", content: "{" }`) as the last message. MODEL_PRIMARY is now
+  `claude-sonnet-5`, which rejects assistant prefill (the route's own comment says so: "no more
+  assistant prefill is used because newer Claude models reject it"). The API call fails, and
+  /api/dasha returns 500 "Dasha prediction failed".
+- Fix: remove the prefill. (Change from the first plan: I kept the call inline and mocked the SDK
+  in the test, because lib/claude-models.test.ts inspects the inline `messages.create(` calls.)
+  Read the reply through `jsonReplyText` (which also reports max_tokens truncation clearly).
+  The route already runs `prepareJsonString`, which extracts the outermost JSON object.
+- Test: new lib/claude-dasha-request.test.ts checks the request ends on a user turn, has no
+  assistant prefill, and keeps thinking set explicitly.
+
+## Log
+
+### Change 1 — lib/claude.ts: remove assistant prefill from generateDashaPrediction; return via jsonReplyText
+### Change 2 — add lib/claude-dasha-request.test.ts (mocks @anthropic-ai/sdk)
+
